      "narration": "Theo markets a group plan to Priya and then helps her explain it to employees. The same truth-in-advertising rules apply: materials must be accurate, name the insurer, and present limitations as clearly as benefits. Enrollment meetings, brochures and the certificate itself are advertising for this purpose, and the insurer is responsible for them. Employer communications that oversell the plan can create liability for benefits the plan does not provide. The summary of benefits and coverage uses a standard format precisely so employees can compare plans without marketing spin.",
